id: pm-oz9jxn
title: "The SDK surface gate classifies every signature text change as breaking, so an optional field added to a host-built context needs the same acknowledgement as a removed export"
description: "Found while landing pm-wb6ktl (2026-11-16). scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs compares each exported symbol's printed signature text, and any difference is reported as breaking. Adding an optional, host-set field to BeforeMutationHookContext was reported as breaking. That context is built by the host and handed to guards, and no implementer constructs it, so no consumer is affected. As a result, an additive SDK change needs the same recorded acknowledgement as a removed export. The gate's own acceptance criteria (pm-e6tm5c) classify changes as additive, compatible or breaking, but no signature change is ever classed as compatible. The cost is that breaking_acknowledgements fill with false positives, which hides the real breaks that reviewers and release notes must see. Some widenings are genuinely breaking, so the classifier must not over-correct. During the same PR, widening runRegisteredMutationGuardForTest from Promise<void> to a value-bearing promise broke consumers that return it from a Promise<void> function (TS2322). An optional property added to a type the caller supplies breaks a caller value that already carries a same-named property of an incompatible type. Proposal: classify signature changes by position and kind, and record the reason with each change. These are compatible: a new optional property on a type only the host constructs; an optional property added to a caller-supplied type when no caller can already carry a same-named, differently typed property; a plain void return widened; a parameter made optional. These stay breaking: removed exports or properties; a new required property on a caller-supplied type; an added optional property that can conflict with a caller's existing same-named property; a Promise<void> or other non-plain-void return widened to a value-bearing type; a narrowed input. Duplicate check: searched sdk surface snapshot breaking signature optional property additive. pm-e6tm5c (closed) delivered the gate; no open item covers classification precision."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[5]: "area:sdk",contracts,developer-experience,release-notes,sdk-surface
created_at: "2026-11-16T04:20:04.606Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T06:15:52.370Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "An optional property on a host-constructed type, or on a caller-supplied type where no caller can already hold a conflicting same-named property, is classified compatible; An added optional property that can conflict with a same-named, differently typed property a caller value already carries is classified breaking, with one spec example; Only a plain void return widening is compatible; widening Promise<void> or another return to a value-bearing type is breaking; A removed export, a removed property or a new required property on a caller-supplied type stays breaking; Each classified change records the reason the classifier used, and the spec covers one example of each class"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: medium
severity: low
expected_result: Only caller-visible incompatibilities require a breaking acknowledgement
actual_result: "Any signature text difference, including an added optional field, is reported as breaking"
